From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:44:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] game: resplit Nintendo Switch Sports Resort shader map

Packing v65536 stops at the shader split table check after PR #2943 made the BAHS split filter candidates outside validated binary record slots.

This updates dm/games/04008E001F098000/shader_map.tsv from a fresh split of v65536. It drops two stray BAHS candidates in agl_technique_pfx.sharcb (16d1e80284e796bd at 0x1c78d4 and 1c90215ef8a46302 at 0x23a21c), shifts the remaining 116 vs_agl.bin rows after them, and updates 22 main BNSH #var source ordering entries. The other 11,057 shaders keep the same keys, shader_facts.tsv, shader_pairs.tsv, and pso_pairs.tsv are unchanged, and no profile table references the two removed keys.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#3081
Reason: Resplit 04008E001F098000 shader_map.tsv for current shader_split.py BAHS bounds filter
Issue: none

---
 dm/games/04008E001F098000/README.md      |   3 +-
 dm/games/04008E001F098000/shader_map.tsv | 308 +++++++++++------------
 2 files changed, 155 insertions(+), 156 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/04008E001F098000/README.md b/dm/games/04008E001F098000/README.md
index 644fa7c..e231b0f 100644
--- a/dm/games/04008E001F098000/README.md
+++ b/dm/games/04008E001F098000/README.md
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ There is no game-specific patch and no rewriter cut. Everything else it needed i
 
 ## Shaders
 
-- 11,059 shaders (`Nin_Ounce_NVN2` BNSH) in [`shader_map.tsv`](shader_map.tsv); a full Mac build takes about 9 minutes on the M6, 4:46 for a second one.
+- 11,057 shaders (`Nin_Ounce_NVN2` BNSH) in [`shader_map.tsv`](shader_map.tsv); a full Mac build takes about 9 minutes on the M6, 4:46 for a second one.
 - 6 are refused (4 task, 2 mesh shaders of the sea, agl `AnnaSea`): their task payloads (21-28 KB) are past Metal's 16 KB ([issue #1753](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/1753); FifteenPen's [PR #2264](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2264) passes them through a device buffer). No draw has been seen to use them.
 - 612 pixel shaders read the fragment's shading-rate size; until it read 1 x 1 the sea and the avatars' hair and clothes were black ([The fragment's shading-rate size reads 1 x 1](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#the-fragments-shading-rate-size-reads-1-x-1)).
 - [`pso_manifest.tsv`](pso_manifest.tsv) is this Mac's own list (3,474 shaders, 1,868 render, 41 compute and 22 task / mesh pipelines): a first start, the menus and a doubles match. The pull requests' lists were recorded by an older host: none of their render or mesh pipeline keys matches the current one's.
@@ -93,3 +93,4 @@ Raw-pointer discovery validation (2026-11-17, Apple M6, macOS 27.2): main `2925d
 - [Tests of one uniform word folded into switches](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#tests-of-one-uniform-word-folded-into-switches) and [Specialized second functions in the offline pipeline archive](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#specialized-second-functions-in-the-offline-pipeline-archive)
 - [A console's own Mii database and system data](../../../docs/reference/services.md#a-consoles-own-mii-database-and-system-data): its Mii heads come from the Switch 2's own archive, `0400000000000849`.
 - [An original Joy-Con's sensors are read by the host](../../../docs/reference/services.md#an-original-joy-cons-sensors-are-read-by-the-host)
+- [A control section's words read as a BAHS entry](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#a-control-sections-words-read-as-a-bahs-entry): the record-based BAHS split of [PR #2943](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2943) drops two stray candidates in `agl_technique_pfx.sharcb` (`16d1e80284e796bd` at `0x1c78d4` and `1c90215ef8a46302` at `0x23a21c`) and reorders 22 `main` BNSH `#var` sources in [`shader_map.tsv`](shader_map.tsv), while `shader_facts.tsv`, `shader_pairs.tsv`, and `pso_pairs.tsv` stay unchanged.
